#{\footnote # display}${\footnote $ Changing the Display}K{\footnote K Changing the Display}+{\footnote + procedures:010}
\pard\sb120\sa120\li120{\b\fs28 Changing the Display}\par
\pard\li120\sa120 Choose Change System Settings, select a display and choose OK. The setting is saved in SYSTEM.INI and takes effect after restarting Interface Manager.\par
\page
#{\footnote # applications}${\footnote $ Setting Up Applications}K{\footnote K Setting Up Applications}+{\footnote + procedures:020}
\pard\sb120\sa120\li120{\b\fs28 Setting Up Applications}\par
\pard\li120\sa120 Choose Set Up Applications and the drives to search. Setup lists the applications it finds; choose those to add, and they appear in Program Manager's Applications and DOS Applications groups.\par
